      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 228,
      "text": "MEXICO\nFUND RELATIONS\n(As of August 31, 2022)\nThe 2022 Article IV discussions were held in Mexico City during September 12—23, 2022. The\nteam comprised Thomas Helbling (head), Jean-Marc Fournier, Swarnali Ahmed Hannan and Kevin\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 228,
      "end_char": 419,
      "text": "Wiseman (all WHD), Carolina Claver (LEG), Samir Jahan (FAD), Faezeh Raei and Misa Takebe (SPR),\nand Jeffrey Williams (MCM). Nigel Chalk and Gaston Gelos (WHD) and Vikram Haksar (FSAP Mission\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 419,
      "end_char": 608,
      "text": "Chief, MCM) attended the concluding meetings. Alfonso Guerra (OED) also participated. The team\nmet with Finance Secretary Ramírez de la O, Governor Rodríguez Ceja, Labor Secretary Alcalde,\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 608,
      "end_char": 803,
      "text": "Economy Secretary Clouthier, other government officials, and representatives of the financial and\nprivate sectors. The team was supported by Boele Bonthuis (FAD), Laila Azoor, Hugo Tuesta (WHD),\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 803,
      "end_char": 972,
      "text": "and Mengqi Wang (2021 summer intern, University of Wisconsin-Madison).\nMexico has accepted the obligations of Article VIII, sections 2, 3, and 4. Comprehensive economic\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 972,
      "end_char": 1196,
      "text": "data are available for Mexico on a timely basis and economic data are adequate for surveillance. It\nsubscribes to the SDDS.\nMembership Status: Joined December 31, 1945\nGeneral Resources Account: SDR Million Percent of Quota\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1196,
      "end_char": 1428,
      "text": "Quota 8,912.70 100.00\nFund holdings of currency 6,345.22 71.19\nReserve position in Fund 2,567.51 28.81\nNew Arrangement to Borrow 3 3 . 7 9\nSDR Department: SDR Million Percent of Allocation\nNet cumulative allocation 11,393.62 100.00\n"
    },
    {
